===Etymology 1===

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+|наде́л}}

# {{lb|ru|historical}} Allotment land, which was the designation for pieces of land granted to peasants by their former landlords and the state with the reforms of the 1860s. The allotment lands had minimum and maximum sizes and were usually collectively owned.

